From f606286e75d4eb3ea0327ab43b418f7393121cf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yanny57 <duke57883@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:35:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] CameraClient: Support legacy MediaTek HAL1 blobs

- MTK HAL1 delivers JPEGs as MTK_CAMERA_MSG_EXT_DATA (0x80000000): an
  ext type (0x10 = compressed image), a shot index and, for multi-image
  shots such as HDR, an is-final flag, followed by the JPEG. Unwrap it
  into CAMERA_MSG_COMPRESSED_IMAGE that points at the JPEG in the same
  heap. These HALs never send CAMERA_MSG_SHUTTER, so deliver one ahead
  of the JPEG, and drop MTK_CAMERA_MSG_EXT_NOTIFY (0x40000000).
  Without this no photo is ever saved.
- Refuse VIDEO_BUFFER_MODE_DATA_CALLBACK_METADATA. The HAL fills the
  metadata buffers with a vendor layout only the MTK OMX encoders read,
  and Codec2 encoders accept only ANW metadata, so configure() failed
  with EINVAL. CameraSource then falls back to YUV callbacks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ic8f9cb3a2e585fe9a2e97f099444f563838318a7
---
